# 🐧 Linux Basics

## Overview

Linux is an open-source operating system widely used in servers, software development, networking, and embedded systems.

I am learning Linux practically using **Ubuntu on WSL** and the Linux terminal.

---

## 📌 Basic Linux Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `pwd` | Shows the Present Working Directory |
| `ls` | Lists files and directories |
| `mkdir` | Creates a new directory |
| `cd` | Changes the current directory |
| `man` | Opens the manual/documentation of a command |
| `date` | Displays the current date and time |
| `whoami` | Displays the current logged-in username |
| `echo` | Displays text in the terminal |
| `history` | Shows previously executed commands |
| `clear` | Clears the terminal screen |
